  "_ambient_floor_note": "doc 06 §2.6(z) / doc 92 §18 (audit 91 D-6). Every rate above is PER ASSET — per 1000 residents, per node, per kilometre, per intersection — and report 98 R-11/R-13 calibrated them against a city that HAS those assets. The founding city has 144 residents and 18 transformer nodes, so doc 92 §18.1 measures its whole ambient budget at 0.268 incidents/game-day = 1.88/game-week (transformer 0.134, fire 0.083, crime 0.051; 12 seeds x 28 game-days with this block disabled): the dispatch drawer, the picker, the fleet and doc 06's five-tier escalation ladder are, at starter scale, close to scenery. Raising the per-asset rates is the wrong lever — report 98 calibrated them per asset, and a rate that pressures 34 buildings buries 800. The right lever is the one doc 07 §8 already uses for the Director's threat points: a size-independent FLOOR under the rate, as a max(), so a channel whose own inventory already out-generates its floor never sees it and the crossover is CONTINUOUS in city size — no cliff, no branch, no 'small city' mode. Per channel rather than aggregate, so the MIX is authored rather than accidental and each department in the founding roster gets work. Budget 0.40/game-day, UNCHANGED across the Wave-7 five-channel re-split (next note): measured delivery 3.04/game-week over the three channels that had a candidate source (doc 92 §18.3) and 6.62/game-week over the five that do now (§18.6, gate 19) — the ruled 2-4 band was measured while a third of the generator surface was disconnected and needs a fresh ruling. NOTE the max() takes the INSTANTANEOUS lambda, not the daily mean, so transformer_failure gains 40% from a floor below its daily average — doc 06 prices it on (load_ratio/0.70)^3 and that collapses to 0.023 at the 03:00 load clamp. The floor fills troughs; it never touches peaks.",
  "_ambient_floor_coverage_note": "WAVE 7: five of the six generators now carry a row. water_main_break and traffic_accident had none because the floor CANNOT INVENT A TARGET and their candidate sources were the base stubs returning [] — `CityIncidentWorld` overrode neither, so both generated exactly zero at every city size regardless of any rate (doc 92 §18.2, filed as D-14/D-15). Both adapters have landed (`sim/incidents/city_incident_world.gd`), both channels generate, and their rows are authored below. storm_damage still carries no row, for a different and permanent reason: its candidates exist only inside a live doc 07 storm cell, and while one is overhead the player has plenty to answer.",
  "_ambient_floor_wave7_note": "The re-derivation doc 92 §18.2 asked for, measured 12 seeds x 28 game-days per arm on `do_nothing` (the same A/B shape as §18.3). BUDGET UNCHANGED at 0.40/game-day, because §18.2 ruled in advance that 'the two new rows come out of the three existing ones'; only the split moved. Per game-week, floor OFF -> floor ON: crime 0.35 -> 0.73, structure_fire 0.69 -> 0.56, transformer_failure 0.81 -> 1.08, water_main_break 0.58 -> 0.60, traffic_accident 3.58 -> 3.60, storm 0.04; TOTAL 6.06 -> 6.62 (the old three-channel split measured 7.29 and reproduced §18.3's 3.04 on its three channels to within noise). 318/318 resolved, 0 failed, 0 abandoned, 0 destroyed, treasury higher on all twelve seeds than with two dead generators. THE SHARES, and why: crime keeps the largest for doc 92 §18.3's reason (safest channel, self-resolves at tier <= 2, damages nothing, carries the ambient texture) but halves, because the loop now has five channels feeding it rather than three. transformer_failure stays the teaching incident and still fills the 03:00 trough its (load_ratio/0.70)^3 collapses into. structure_fire stays deliberately the rarest — a fire should be an event, not a chore — and its floor is insurance for a SHRUNKEN roster, not a lift on a full one. water_main_break 0.06 gives the two founding water trucks their first ambient work: at starter scale the natural rate (1.56 km of mains) already reads 0.083/day so the floor does not bind, and it is there for a city with one lateral. traffic_accident takes the SMALLEST share, 0.04, because it is the one channel whose asset base doc 09 hands the player complete at t0 — 389 junctions against 34 buildings — so its natural rate (0.515/day, still BELOW doc 06 2.6(e)'s own worked intent of 0.687/day) dwarfs any floor at every city size that has roads; the row exists only for a hand-built city that does not yet.",
  "ambient_floor": {
    "enabled": true,
    "grace_days": 2.0,
    "per_day": {
      "crime": 0.14,
      "structure_fire": 0.08,
      "transformer_failure": 0.08,
      "water_main_break": 0.06,
      "traffic_accident": 0.04
    }
  },
